WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.680
Netflix is dropping more than a few exciting
new releases this November.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.269
The final season of House of Cards is making
its debut this month, along with the Chris

00:00:09.269 --> 00:00:10.480
Pine-led The Outlaw King.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.260
And that's just the tip of the iceberg.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.860
Here's everything good coming to Netflix in
November 2018.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.780
Even though Kevin Spacey's out of the picture,
his character, Frank Underwood, will apparently

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:24.600
still play into the events of the final season
of House of Cards.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.160
According to Reuters, the exact cause of his
death will be something of a lingering mystery

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.900
that's sticking around to haunt his widow
and the new president, Claire Underwood.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.440
Check it out when House of Cards returns on
November 2nd.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:41.100
Journey back to the clashing cultures of 1970
with ReMastered: Tricky Dick &amp; The Man in

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.270
Black, a documentary about that time Johnny
Cash went to the White House to hang out with

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.200
Richard Nixon.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.449
This is the second installment in Netflix's
musical documentary series, the first of which,

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:56.900
ReMastered: Who Shot the Sheriff, delved into
the 1976 assassination attempt on Bob Marley.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.380
Look for Tricky Dick &amp; The Man in Black on
November 2nd.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:04.920
Only in 2018 would the epic unfinished film
by legendary director Orson Welles go straight

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:05.740
to streaming.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.740
But here we are, on the cusp of the Netflix
release of a film over 40 years in the making.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.900
Welles supposedly left behind ten hours of
raw footage for his satirical mockumentary,

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:20.040
and it's now been painstakingly edited together
into a finished product.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.430
The Other Side of the Wind premieres on November
2nd, side-by-side with They'll Love Me When

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.620
I'm Dead, a documentary that explores the
making of the film.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:33.460
In this one-man show, John Leguizamo delivers
a comedy filled stage drama that traces Latin

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.760
history from the Mayans to the modern day.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:40.960
The show garnered Leguizamo a Tony nomination
for best play, and Netflix brought their cameras

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.660
to capture one of the acclaimed performances
in June 2018.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.900
Tune in to John Leguizamo's Latin History
for Morons on November 5th.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:54.240
Chris Pine stars in this upcoming Netflix
film as Robert the Bruce, the real-life historical

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.100
figure who organized the Scottish clans to
go to war against England.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.520
From the looks of the trailers so far, Outlaw
King will be a bloody romp through history

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.960
that tracks Robert's path from fugitive to
King of Scots.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.060
Take a look on November 9th.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:12.240
Halloween certainly doesn't mark the end of
the year's horror releases, as Netflix's upcoming

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.700
May The Devil Take You proves.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.280
The Indonesian fright flick focuses on a young
woman who travels to her father's old house

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.900
after he falls into a coma.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:24.540
There, she discovers that dear old dad had
more than a few skeletons in his closet — and

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.020
some of them want to kill her.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.720
Get ready for a dark descent into hell when
May The Devil Take You hits Netflix on November

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.280
15th.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:36.160
You probably won't recognize Madeline Brewer's
name, but her face may ring a bell.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.040
The young actress appeared in Orange is the
New Black, The Handmaid's Tale, and Black

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:44.520
Mirror, and now she's set to star in Netflix's
newest psychological thriller, Cam.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:49.000
The film follows Alice, a webcam girl whose
life is hijacked by someone who looks just

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:49.620
like her.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.840
That kicks off a harrowing mystery as Alice
tries to figure out what her doppelganger

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:54.860
wants from her.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.680
Check it out on November 16th.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.760
The Narcos spin-off Narcos: Mexico puts a
new cast of characters at the start of the

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.650
Mexican drug war, setting the series in the
early '80s and chronicling the bloody beginnings

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:07.960
of a violent cartel.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.710
Michael Pena and Diego Luna are set to star,
and the new take on the series looks like

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.790
it'll be downright brutal but also pretty
amazing.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.260
Dig in on November 16.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:22.060
There's been a lot of hype building for The
Ballad of Buster Scruggs, the newest release

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.460
from Joel and Ethan Coen.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:28.930
The anthology film twines together six different
stories about the American West, each infused

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:32.380
with the kind of dark comedy that could only
come from the Coen brothers.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:37.480
Buster Scruggs has already hit the 2018 festival
circuit, and critics are loving it.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.180
Will the rest of the world fall in love too?

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:42.240
Find out when it rides onto Netflix on November
16th.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:47.140
Among all the historical shows on Netflix,
The Last Kingdom tends to fall between the

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:47.640
cracks.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.520
That's a shame, because this period epic is
definitely worth the time to watch.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.740
Originally created by BBC, The Last Kingdom
follows a warrior in the 9th century during

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:00.380
a time when what is now England was being
overrun by the invading Danes.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:05.071
Between its high production values, solid
storytelling, and breathtaking battles, The

00:04:05.071 --> 00:04:08.010
Last Kingdom is definitely worth checking
out.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.420
Season 3 hits Netflix on November 19th.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.960
Not to be confused with that other show about
the Archie comics character, this Sabrina

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:19.049
is a horror film about a doll that comes to
life after a little girl tries to bring her

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:20.360
mother back from the dead.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:24.540
That's a cheerful premise, and the trailer
for Sabrina suggests that it only gets worse

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.180
from there.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.440
Look for it to hit Netflix on November 20th.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:33.340
The 2017 return of Mystery Science Theater
3000 gave fans plenty to love.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:37.570
All the charm of the old series was back,
along with a brand new set of terrible films

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.570
to make fun of.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.300
What's not to like?

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:43.760
With the next season, Jonah and his robo-friends
will be riffing on six new movies.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.500
Grab your popcorn and settle in for the new
season on November 22nd.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.640
Between The Last Kingdom and Frontier, Netflix
is bringing plenty of historical action to

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.220
the small screen in November.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:58.500
Frontier is set in the Canadian frontier and
follows an outlaw who's dead set on wreaking

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:00.360
havoc on the region's fur trade.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.400
That outlaw is Declan Harp, played by Jason
Momoa.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:07.440
Whether you're a longtime fan or just now
getting into Frontier, you can look forward

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.280
to Season 3 when it arrives on November 23rd.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:15.660
Netflix has two new standup specials slated
for November, and each one is well worth a

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.160
watch.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.940
On the 20th, watch out for Trevor Noah: Son
of Patricia, which sees The Daily Show host

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.160
on-stage for an evening of hard-hitting jokes.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:28.180
Then, November 27th heralds the arrival of
a double dose of comedy, when Jeff Ross and

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:33.330
Dave Attell both take the stage and take turns
roasting each other in a special called Bumping

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.140
Mics with Jeff Ross &amp; Dave Attell.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.180
That's all of the good Netflix originals coming
in November.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.720
Now let's highlight a few of the best films
hitting the streaming service.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:47.320
Alfonso Cuaron's excellent Children of Men
is the highlight of November's action additions,

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.100
arriving on the first.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:52.520
The dystopian drama follows a disillusioned
alcoholic who's roped into protecting the

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.280
last known pregnant woman on Earth.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:59.400
Cuaron used extensive long takes while filming,
leading to some pretty jaw-dropping action

00:05:59.400 --> 00:05:59.900
scenes.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:04.780
After that, look for Pirates of the Caribbean:
At World's End to sail onto streaming on November

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:05.280
4th.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:09.400
There's also a flood of irreverent comedies
splashing onto Netflix on the first.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:14.840
Look for Deuce Bigalow: European Gigolo, National
Lampoon's Animal House, and Scary Movie 2

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:15.340
and 3.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:19.280
It might not be a high-brow selection, but
it's bound to be high-larious.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:21.640
I can’t believe I just said that, Haha.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:25.860
On the thriller side, Netflix is doubling
down on its post-Halloween chills.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:31.570
On the first, keep your eyes open for Cloverfield,
From Dusk Till Dawn, Bram Stoker's Dracula,

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:32.520
and Transcendence.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:36.870
On the 12th, Netflix is checking in Green
Room, an intense little movie about a band

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.120
stuck in a gig full of murderous neo-Nazis.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:43.560
Anton Yelchin stars, with a sinister performance
by Patrick Stewart as the villain.

